core: add image attachment support with byte-bounded normalization

Let users attach images to a turn via /image. Attached images are
decoded, downscaled to a bounding box, and re-encoded to JPEG under a
byte cap so the base64 payload stays bounded in the context window and
the durable transcript, mirroring Pi's autoResizeImages. Providers
serialize image blocks per-API, models opt in via supports_image, and a
byte-pressure guard stops and compacts when total image bytes exceed
the request budget.
